content.text:
New game mobile layout is broken: starter cards in horizontal layout place description in narrow right column, causing tall narrow text and stats clipping off the right. The screenshot shows starter card row with sprite, name, then description narrow column and stats partially off-screen (HP/ATK... clipped). Need fix responsive starter card: don't use horizontal layout; use vertical/grid better.

Current mobile CSS:
```
.starter-grid { grid-template-columns:1fr }
.starter-card { flex-direction: row; text-align:left; align-items:center; }
.starter-card .starter-art { min-height:64 }
.starter-card .starter-art img {62px}
```
The card is a button with several children in a column flex (name, badge, desc, stats). Row direction makes all children side by side! That's why. Need change starter card layout to grid or keep column. Easiest: remove horizontal; keep column but more compact with sprite on left? Could restructure CSS with grid:
```
.starter-card { display:grid; grid-template-columns: 72px 1fr; grid-template-areas: "art name" "art badge" "art copy" "stats stats"; text-align:left; align-items:center; gap: 4px 10px; }
```
But the card markup order: select-mark span, starter-art div, strong, elementBadge (div), span.starter-copy, div.starter-stats. CSS grid areas need assign classes; strong can target. Simpler: revert to column (default) and make art min-height 64, overall compact. Then cards are tall but readable and scrollable. The modal body scrolls; okay. Each card ~200px; fine.

At mobile:
```
.starter-card { flex-direction: column; text-align: center; align-items: center; padding: 10px; }
.starter-card .starter-art { min-height: 56px; }
```
That was the default. So remove the horizontal overrides. But the default `.starter-card` is flex column? Check base styles.

