Now run smoke script. We'll use run-code to add pageerror listener, open each screen via app methods, wait, close by clicking .close-btn, then open menu/settings/help, and test battle by constructing one; return errors and state. Need to be careful with modal close timing.

Script:
```
async page => {
 const errors=[];
 page.on('pageerror', e=>errors.push(String(e)));
 const res = await page.evaluate(async () => {
   const a=window.__AETHERIA__;
   const wait=ms=>new Promise(r=>setTimeout(r,ms));
   const out=[];
   const open=async name=>{ a[name](); await wait(60); out.push([name, !!document.querySelector('.screen-panel')]); document.querySelector('.close-btn')?.click(); await wait(220); };
   await open('openParty'); await open('openDex'); await open('openBag'); await open('openMap'); await open('openQuests'); await open('openMenu');
   // menu settings sub-screen
   a.openMenu(); await wait(60);
   [...document.querySelectorAll('.screen-foot button, .menu-actions button')].find(b=>b.textContent.includes('Settings'))?.click(); await wait(80);
   out.push(['settings', !!document.querySelector('.screen-panel')]);
   document.querySelector('.close-btn')?.click(); await wait(200);
   ...
   return out;
 });
 await page.waitForTimeout(400);
 return {res, errors};
}
```
`openSettings` directly exists; use it, openHelp too.

Also test dialogue NPC: `a.screens.talkTo(a.world.nearestNpc?)` difficult. We can test battle engine directly via UI startWildBattle; then perform one turn action via clicking .move-btn; wait 2s; then run.

